<span id="Description"></span>
==Описание==

Инструментът [[Image:PartDesign_Pad.svg|24px]] '''Протрузия (PartDesign Pad)''' създава твърдо тяло в активния обект Тяло чрез екструдиране на скица, 2D обект или едно или повече лица по прав път. Формата му е съчетана със съществуващото твърдо тяло, ако има предишни функции.

[[File:PartDesign Pad example.svg|none]]

{{Caption|Скица (А) отляво; краен резултат след работа с протрузия (B) отдясно}}

<span id="Usage"></span>
==Използване==

# Изберете една скица или подобен 2D обект, или едно или повече лица от една скица или друг обект, или от самото Тяло.
# Има няколко начина да се позовете на инструмента:
#* Натиснете бутон {{Button|[[Image:PartDesign_Pad.svg|16px]] [[PartDesign_Pad/bg|Протрузия]]}}.
#* Изберете от манюто {{MenuCommand|Part Design → Добавящи функции → [[Image:PartDesign_Pad.svg|16px]] Протрузия}}.
# Отваря се панелът на задачите.
# Задайте параметрите, вижте [[#Options|Опции]] по-долу. {{Version|1.1}}: Ако е отметнато {{MenuCommand|Show interactive draggers when editing features}} [[PartDesign_Preferences/bg#General|предпочитание]] (по подразбиране), параметрите на дължината и ъгъла на заостряне могат да се регулират с интерактивни gizmos в [[3D_View/bg|3D rph.eod]].
# Натиснете бутона {{Button|Добре}}, за да затворите панела на задачата и да завършите действието на инструмента.
# Функция Pad се появява в активното тяло.

<span id="Editing"></span>
==Редактиране==

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
The Pad can be edited after its creation in two ways:
* Double-clicking it in the [[Tree_View|Tree View]], or by right-clicking and selecting '''Edit Pad''' in the context menu; this brings up the task panel and ({{Version|1.1}}) the interactive gizmos (if enabled).
* Via the [[Property_View|Property View]].
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
==Options==
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
The task panel offers the following settings:
</div>

[[Image:PartDesign_Pad_Taskpanel.png|frame]]

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
=== Start ===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
{{Version|26.3}}
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Sets where the pad begins. By default the pad starts at the sketch or face used as its profile.
* '''Profile plane''' (default): the pad starts directly at the profile's sketch plane or face.
* '''Offset''': the pad starts at a numerical distance from the profile, entered in the '''Offset''' field.
* '''Reference''': the pad starts at a face, [[Part_DatumPlane|datum plane]], or sketch selected with the {{Button|Pick Reference}} button.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
This is useful to create multiple features from a single master sketch without needing separate offset planes for each one.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
===Direction===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
{{Version|1.1}} (as ''Mode'')
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Sets the direction(s) of the pad:
* '''One sided''': the pad extends on one side of the sketch or face.
* '''Two sided''': the pad extends on both sides of the sketch or face. Two sub-menus (''Side 1'' and ''Side 2'') appear to define the pad for each side.
* '''Symmetric''': the pad is symmetrical with respect to the original sketch or face.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
===Type===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
''For Side 1 and Side 2 if applicable.''
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Offers five ways to specify the length of the pad:
* '''Dimension''': enter a numeric value for the '''Length''' of the pad. With the '''Direction''' option '''Symmetric''' the pad will extend half the given length to either side of the sketch or face.
* '''To last''': the pad will extend up to the last face of the support it encounters in its direction. If there is no support, an error message will appear.
* '''To first''': the pad will extend up to the first face of the support it encounters in its direction. If there is no support, an error message will appear.
* '''Up to face''': the pad will extend up to a face. Press the {{Button|Select Face}} button and select a face or a [[Part_DatumPlane|datum plane]] from the Body.
* '''Up to shape''': {{Version|1.0}}: the pad will extend up to the selected shape. Optionally press the {{Button|Select Shape}} button and select a shape. Leave the '''Select all faces''' checkbox enabled or disable it, press the {{Button|Select}} button and select the faces up to which the pad should be created.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
=== Offset to face ===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
''For Side 1 and Side 2 if applicable.''
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Offset from face at which the pad will end. This option is only available if '''Type''' (for the same side) is '''To last''', '''To first''' or '''Up to face'''.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
===Length===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
''For Side 1 and Side 2 if applicable.''
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Defines the length of the pad. This option is only available if '''Type''' (for the same side) is '''Dimension'''.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
=== Taper angle ===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
''For Side 1 and Side 2 if applicable.''
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Tapers the pad in the extrusion direction by the given angle. A positive angle means the outer pad border gets wider. This option is only available if '''Type''' (for the same side) is '''Dimension'''.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
=== Reversed ===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Reverses the direction of the pad.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
=== Direction/edge ===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
You can select the direction of the extrusion:
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* '''Sketch normal''' or '''Face normal:''' The sketch or face is extruded in the direction of its normal. If you have selected several faces to be extruded, the normal of the first one will be used.
* '''Select reference…:''' The sketch or face is extruded in the direction of a straight edge or a [[Part_DatumLine|datum line]] selected from the Body.
* '''Custom direction:''' The sketch or face is extruded in the direction of the specified vector.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
=== Length along sketch normal ===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
Uncheck this option to measure along the specified direction. This option is not available if '''Direction/edge''' is '''Sketch normal''' or '''Face normal'''.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
=== Recompute on change ===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
This option should be checked if '''Show final result''' or '''Show preview overlay''' is checked.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
=== Show final result ===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
If checked the cumulative result of the previous features and the current operation is shown.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
=== Show preview overlay ===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
If checked the result of the current operation is shown as an overlay.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
==Notes==
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* Sketches containing [[B-Splines|B-splines]] often cannot be tapered properly. This is a limitation of the [[OpenCASCADE|OpenCASCADE]] kernel that FreeCAD uses.
* For larger angles tapering will fail if the end face would have fewer edges than the start face/sketch.
* The algorithm used for '''To first''' and '''To last''' is:
** Create a line through the center of gravity of the sketch
** Find all faces of the support cut by this line
** Choose the face where the intersection point is nearest/furthest from the sketch
: This means that the face that is found might not always be what you expected. If you run into this problem, use the '''Up to face''' type instead, and pick the face you want.
: For the very special case of extrusion to a concave surface, where the sketch is larger than this surface, extrusion will fail. This is an unresolved bug.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
==Properties==
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
See also: [[Property_View|Property View]].
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
A PartDesign Pad object is derived from a [[Part_Feature|Part Feature]] object and inherits all its properties. It also has the following additional properties:
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
===Data===
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
{{TitleProperty|Compatibility}}
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* {{PropertyData|Use Legacy Taper Direction|Bool|Hidden}}: {{Version|26.3}}
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
{{TitleProperty|Pad}}
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* {{PropertyData|Side Type|Enumeration}}: {{Value|One side}}, {{Value|Two sides}} or {{Value|Symmetric}}. {{Version|1.1}}
* {{PropertyData|Use Custom Vector|Bool}}: If checked, the pad direction is based on the {{PropertyData|Direction}} vector instead of the {{PropertyData|Reference Axis}}.
* {{PropertyData|Direction|Vector}}: Vector of the pad direction if {{PropertyData|Use Custom Vector}} is used.
* {{PropertyData|Reference Axis|LinkSub}}: The sketch normal, or an edge or datum line from the body.
* {{PropertyData|Along Sketch Normal|Bool}}: If checked, the pad length is measured along the sketch normal. Otherwise it is measured along the {{PropertyData|Direction}} or {{PropertyData|Reference Axis}}.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
{{TitleProperty|Part Design}}
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* {{PropertyData|Operation|Enumeration|Hidden}}: Not used. {{Version|26.3}}
* {{PropertyData|Refine|Bool}}: If checked, residual edges left after the operation are cleaned up. This property is initially set according to the user's settings (found in {{MenuCommand|Preferences → Part Design → General → Model Settings}}).
* {{PropertyData|Fuzzy Tolerance|FloatConstraint}}: {{Version|1.1}}
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
{{TitleProperty|Side1}}
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* {{PropertyData|Type|Enumeration}}: {{Value|Length}}, {{Value|UpToLast}}, {{Value|UpToFirst}}, {{Value|UpToFace}} or {{Value|UpToShape}}. Do not use {{Value|?TwoLengths}}. Defines how the pad will end.
* {{PropertyData|Length|Length}}: The length of the pad.
* {{PropertyData|Up To Face|LinkSub}}: Face where the pad will end.
* {{PropertyData|Up To Shape|LinkSubList}}: Faces or shape(s) where the pad will end.
* {{PropertyData|Offset|Length}}: Offset from the face where the pad will end. This is only taken into account if the {{PropertyData|Type}} option {{Value|UpToLast}}, {{Value|UpToFirst}} or {{Value|UpToFace}} is used.
* {{PropertyData|Taper Angle|Angle}}: Taper angle of the extrusion.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
{{TitleProperty|Side2}}
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
The properties in this group are only editable if {{PropertyData|Side Type}} is {{Value|Two sides}}. See the '''Side1''' group for more information about the properties.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* {{PropertyData|Type2|Enumeration}}: {{Version|1.1}}
* {{PropertyData|Length2|Length}}
* {{PropertyData|Up To Face2|LinkSub}}: {{Version|1.1}}
* {{PropertyData|Up To Shape2|LinkSubList}}: {{Version|1.1}}
* {{PropertyData|Offset2|Length}}: {{Version|1.1}}
* {{PropertyData|Taper Angle2|Angle}}
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
{{TitleProperty|Sketch Based}}
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* {{PropertyData|Profile|LinkSub}}: Reference to the object or faces the pad is based on.
* {{PropertyData|Midplane|Bool}}: Deprecated, use {{PropertyData|Side Type}} instead.
* {{PropertyData|Reversed|Bool}}: Reverses the direction of the  pad.
* {{PropertyData|Allow Multi Face|Bool}}: If checked, only the first face of {{PropertyData|Profile}} is used. Ignored for sketches and internal faces from sketches.
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
{{TitleProperty|Start}}
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* {{PropertyData|Start Type|Enumeration}}: {{Value|Profile plane}}, {{Value|Offset}} or {{Value|Reference}}. Sets how the start of the pad is defined. {{Version|26.3}}
* {{PropertyData|Start Offset|Length}}: Distance between the profile and the start of the pad. Not used if {{PropertyData|Start Type}} is '''Profile plane'''. {{Version|26.3}}
* {{PropertyData|Start Reference|LinkSub}}: A face, plane, or sketch the pad starts from. Only used if {{PropertyData|Start Type}} is '''Reference'''. {{Version|26.3}}
</div>


